(Clinical Reference: Pharmacology Overview & Safe Medication Use) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(1. Common Cardiometabolic Drug Classes) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Biguanides \(e.g., Metformin\): First-line insulin-sensitizing agent for type 2 diabetes.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(ACE Inhibitors \(e.g., Lisinopril\) & ARBs \(e.g., Losartan\): First-line antihypertensive therapy.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(HMG-CoA Reductase Inhibitors \(Statins e.g., Atorvastatin, Rosuvastatin\): Lipid-lowering agents.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Beta-Blockers \(e.g., Metoprolol\): Regulate heart rate and myocardial oxygen demand.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(2. Adherence, Safety, and Monitoring) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Medications must be taken strictly as prescribed by a licensed healthcare professional.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Do not abruptly discontinue cardiovascular or metabolic medications without medical consultation.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Regular monitoring of renal function, electrolytes, and hepatic enzymes is standard clinical practice.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(3. Adverse Effects and Warning Symptoms) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Common side effects: Gastrointestinal upset with Metformin, dry cough with ACE inhibitors, myalgia with statins.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Severe adverse reactions \(e.g. angioedema, jaundice, severe hypoglycemia\) require immediate medical care.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Inform healthcare providers of all over-the-counter supplements and herbal products.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(4. Patient-Doctor Communication Essentials) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Maintain an up-to-date medication list including dosages and schedules.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Report any suspected adverse reactions or difficulty affording prescriptions promptly to the provider.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(MedSafe does not recommend changing, adjusting, or initiating any pharmaceutical regimen.) Tj
T*
T*
